-- The build tool as a package — the one whose descriptor the tool itself has to be able to read, and
-- as of v0.2 of the toolchain the one it can build.
--
-- **Three packages, no scopes, no tasks, every one of them written out.** `root` is the library at `src/`, which
-- is what a consumer would get by naming `//root`; it says `at .` because its directory is the
-- repository's own and its name would have said otherwise. The name is a convention and nothing more. `launcher` is that library plus a platform
-- plus an entry point, and `test` is the suite at `test/src`. Nothing depends on either, so neither
-- one's platform layer reaches anybody — the isolation the old `artifact` and `test` scopes were
-- enforcing is the shape of the graph now (`docs/build-system.md`, "What this replaced, and why").
--
-- **What a build runs is one `compiler` line per package in the closure** (`docs/build-system.md`,
-- "What a build runs"). `launcher` carries its own: build the executable, don't run it. `test` carries
-- none — `eliot-test//suite` carries `compiler run -m eliot.test.Runner`, so `eliot test`
-- compiles the suite and runs it, and fails when a case does. Neither line is on `root`, and neither
-- could be: every closure holding `root` would run it, the other leaf among them.
--
-- `//stdlib` alone in the root package, because that is what `src` names: `eliot.collection.List`,
-- `eliot.file` and `eliot.system`. The `lang` layer arrives underneath it anyway — the eliot
-- repository's own descriptor says `package stdlib { dep //lang }` — and a dependency this package
-- does not import is not this package's to declare.
--
-- `v0.20`, everywhere, with eliot-test `v0.8`, the eliot-test tag on it: eliot's capability passing (D36, `v0.17`)
-- with its handles erased (`v0.18`), compiled in parallel (`v0.19`, whose warm rebuilds `v0.20` fixes). eliot-test
-- `v0.6` was the first tag whose `mocked` binds its doubles with a `with` around its run of the code rather than on its
-- slot, which eliot `v0.15` and later require.
-- D36's scope check reads a row alias's entries exactly, so a definition that performs fewer than an alias names
-- writes its clause out (`cachedDescriptorTextAt`).
-- `v0.11` with eliot-test `v0.5` was the pin as the first eliot tag that reads `uses *` on a definition taking
-- `uses *` code (D24), which `test` writes, and the first eliot-test tag written that way. Eliot `v0.9` is the
-- first tag with the `uses` surface `src` and `test` are written in, and `v0.10` the first whose compiler compiles
-- eliot-test `v0.4`, whose doubles raise `IoError` on `mocked`'s
-- slot; eliot-test `v0.4` is also the first written in `uses`. `v0.4` is the first eliot tag whose compiler has the `run` mode and picks the
-- backend by it (the `compiler` lines here name none), and whose descriptor names its assets with
-- `asset`, the only spelling this tool reads; `v0.5` is the first whose warm build over an unchanged
-- tree stays warm rather than alternating with a slow one; `v0.6` is the first with `--progress`, which the
-- launcher passes every compiler it runs; `v0.7` is the first whose base has `when`/`unless`, `someIf`,
-- `filterMap`/`findMap`, `includes`, `Eq[Option]` and `first`/`second`, which `src` is written with, and
-- the first whose compiler emits two `if..else`s over two kinds of `Option` without one losing its
-- `runAbort`. `eliot-test v0.2` is the first with `//suite`, and `v0.3` the first with `recordCall`, which
-- `TableGit` journals its operations with, and `whenSpawningWrites`, which `ShellAssetsTests` arranges the
-- archive a mocked `curl` leaves with — its `delete` refuses a path nothing is at, as the platform does.

-- The launcher `./eliotw` runs, and the one line of this file the wrapper reads: it greps for the first
-- line starting `launcher `. The launcher itself accepts the line and ignores it.
launcher v0.7

package root {
  at .
  dep github.com/eliotlang/eliot//stdlib v0.20
}

package launcher {
  dep //root
  dep github.com/eliotlang/eliot//jvm v0.20
  compiler exe-jar -m eliot.build.Launcher
}

package test {
  dep //root
  dep github.com/eliotlang/eliot-test//suite v0.8
  dep github.com/eliotlang/eliot//jvm v0.20
}
